UID:4baa724bc30ff71e@role-family-law.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260724T194435Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260724
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine’s 6th Annual Wild Blueberry Weekend
DESCRIPTION:Hello\, this is Governor Janet Mills\, and thank you for liste
 ning.\nRecently\, I was proud to\nproclaim\nAugust 1 and 2\, 2026\, as Mai
 ne's 6th annual Wild Blueberry Weekend. We do this to celebrate our wild b
 lueberries\, of course\, and in honor of the hard-working people who grow 
 and bring Maine blueberries to markets near and far.\nThe Wabanaki Nations
  in Maine were the first to harvest wild blueberries. In recent history\, 
 the Passamaquoddy Wild Blueberry Company\, headquartered in Columbia Falls
  and owned and operated by the Passamaquoddy Tribe\, has been managing and
  harvesting wild blueberries on 2\,000 acres of blueberry barrens.\nLast y
 ear alone\, Maine farmers harvested 55 million pounds of wild blueberries.
  This special fruit has more antioxidants and is much tastier than any oth
 er kind of blueberry in the world.\nTo honor our wild blueberry growers an
 d businesses and their significant contributions to the Maine economy\, I 
 declared our first-ever Wild Blueberry Weekend in 2021. Wild blueberry gro
 wers opened their doors and made fresh\, wild blueberry jams and pies and 
 other products for guests to purchase. The Wild Blueberry Commission of Ma
 ine reported that there were thousands of dollars in direct farm sales and
  thousands of visitors who enjoyed touring the places where wild blueberri
 es grow\, maybe even picking a few of their own.\nWell\, this year\, the 6
 th annual Wild Blueberry Weekend will feature farm tours and other family-
 friendly activities at 11 different farms in Cumberland\, Hancock\, Kenneb
 ec\, Knox\, Lincoln\, and Washington counties\, as well as at the Wild Blu
 eberry Heritage Center in Columbia Falls. And wild blueberry-themed menu i
 tems and products will be available throughout the weekend at restaurants\
 , ice cream shops\, breweries\, wineries\, and distilleries all across the
  state.\nTo see the full list of participants\, visit\nwww.wildblueberrywe
 ekend.com\nand\nwww.realmaine.com\nfor year-round ideas on ways you can su
 pport Maine’s agriculture community. I encourage every\nhttp://www.maine
 .gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/maines-6th-annual-wild-blueberry-we
 ekend-2026-07-24
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/news/radio_address/maines-6th-annu
 al-wild-blueberry-weekend-2026-07-24
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
